# BUGS

Nothing is drawn or computed on the GPU: the firmware runs and answers, and no command stream group is started.
The power-up is the Sky1's alone.
`power DEVICE off` and `on` in devmgr's `ctl` (devmgr(8)) cut the GPU and bring it back, each time with a new host that probes it, resets it and boots the firmware again.
The job, MMU and GPU interrupts are not served.
devmgr gives a host the first interrupt of its device only, and its handle doesn't say which of the GPU's three lines it is, so every wait is a poll; the firmware's events (idle, faults) go unread, and an MMU fault shows only in the registers a failed step prints.
A GPU reset after the boot, and with it the firmware's reload, is not done: a firmware that stops answering stays stopped until the host is started again.
Every section is mapped write-combining and uncached for the GPU, the MCU's code included, which is slower than the cached mapping the image asks for.
Each section is one contiguous allocation, so a very large one can fail for want of contiguous memory (`FAILED at firmware load`).
The firmware's timers are in GPU_TIMESTAMP ticks, whose rate is measured, not read from the system timer.
The GPU's own DMA, through the stub's BTI, reaches all of memory: nothing confines it beyond its own page tables.
